index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f430f063e3d3b01ee0cd73d04a355f6bb0d2e684
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/relay-outbox.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Optional final-text outbox
+
+`platforms.gadget.extra.enable_relay_outbox: true` enables this experimental service
+only with the matching Hermes final-delivery context hook (version 2). The default
+is false. The owning profile stores private state under
+`plugin_data_dir('gadget')`: `relay-grants.json` and `relay-outbox.sqlite3`. Paths and
+host URLs cannot be supplied by clients. Windows activation is refused pending an
+actual private ACL and parent/reparse verifier.
+
+A paired connection must advertise `caps.relay: {"version": 1}` and have a current
+explicit grant tied to its enrolled key, plus approval from the runner's real
+allowlist callback. Welcome commits that enrollment's opt-in before advertising
+`relay: {"version": 1}`. A stock reconnect opts out. The server pins the key proven
+by HMAC or TOFU; hello fields never establish this provenance. Re-enrollment under
+the same device ID does not inherit the previous owner's finals.
+
+Only `relay.info`, `relay.outbox.read`, and `relay.outbox.ack` are exposed. Read and
+ACK require the current grant on every call. Final text uses durable delivery IDs;
+reads are silent, and neither recordings, approvals, actions nor synthesis are
+replayed. Fresh live speech remains available. Retrying the same accepted input
+returns its original delivery or a conflict, independent of socket epochs and
+answer text. Slash/ephemeral replies keep their ordinary delivery path.
+
+The Hermes hook preserves an adapter-owned identity with the atomic turn marker
+before inference, carries it into the delivery ledger, and lets adapters recover
+final text without calling their ordinary live send interface. A failed outbox or
+ledger write does not report success or release the unresolved turn marker.
+Recovered native events retain the original server-generated input identity.
+The accepted enrollment identity remains separate from a queued or redirected
+terminal input identity. Core handoff atomically updates the marker before
+publishing that terminal identity, and keeps the opening enrollment authority.
+The queued first-response lane binds its synthetic final only from the held
+trusted context or the actual stock opening event; missing opted-in provenance
+fails closed. Recovery of an intermediate queued final cannot release a marker
+while its chain is still executing.
+Context-free legacy recovery is denied while this extension is active because
+its original enrollment cannot be established. Unavailable grant/enrollment
+reads deny access without treating an unreadable registry as authoritative
+revocation. A failed load persists `_enrollment_complete: false` through stock
+writes and subsequent restarts. Ordinary enrollment cannot certify that lost
+owners were intentionally removed. An administrator must restore a complete
+registry and reload it; a new/missing registry likewise needs explicit complete
+initialization before relay activation. Known complete empty registries and
+explicit forget from a complete registry remain authoritative revocations.
+Verified revocation removes retained bodies and opt-ins.
+
+Frames are limited to 65,536 UTF-8 bytes and parser depth 8; final text is at most
+16,384 UTF-8 bytes and must also fit its actual serialized response envelope.
+Pages contain at most 50 items. The outbox keeps the existing 24-hour delivery
+TTL, seven-day identity retention, per-device/profile quotas, and 36 MiB combined
+SQLite/journal disk budget. This does not change canonical Hermes history
+retention. Stop/start follows the owning adapter's lifecycle.
+
+Validation is offline: actual pinned clean/runtime core imports, synthetic
+loopback devices, process restart, and private temporary stores. No live-host,
+provider, physical-device, Windows permission or public-release claim follows.
